<title>SWITZERLAND: Swiss sight deposits rise to 3.78 bln Swiss francs.</title>
<headline>Swiss sight deposits rise to 3.78 bln Swiss francs.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Swiss National Bank said sight deposits rose by 6.6 million Swiss francs to 3.78 billion in the reporting period ended June 10.</p>
<p>Statement of June 11 in millions of Swiss francs:</p>
<p>					 Latest   Change since May 31</p>
<p> Sight deposits		   3,779.5	plus   6.6</p>
<p> Currency reserves	     47,604.5	minus  1,826.3</p>
<p> Domestic securities	    4,867.1	plus   8.5</p>
<p> Notes in circulation	  28,565.8	minus  752.8</p>
<p> Other call deposits		229.3	plus   38.3</p>
<p> Government time deposits     2,500.6	minus  315.9</p>
<p>Borrowing at the emergency Lombard window fell by 2.3 million francs to nil in the reporting period. Outstanding borrowing via the discount facility and swaps of money market certificates rose by 908.3 million francs to 2,506.9 million.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial, +41 1 631 7340</p>
